WEBVTT

00:00:00.673 --> 00:00:01.923
Transitions.

00:00:01.923 --> 00:00:04.728
Name the logic first, then pick the word.

00:00:04.728 --> 00:00:08.438
Do that, and these become some of the fastest points on the test.

00:00:09.977 --> 00:00:11.702
Here's how to spot one.

00:00:11.702 --> 00:00:15.877
A short passage with a blank, usually right at the start of a sentence.

00:00:15.877 --> 00:00:18.186
And four linking words to choose from.

00:00:19.269 --> 00:00:21.044
So what is it really testing?

00:00:21.044 --> 00:00:23.279
The logic between two sentences.

00:00:23.279 --> 00:00:24.744
Not vocabulary.

00:00:24.744 --> 00:00:25.639
Logic.

00:00:26.677 --> 00:00:28.302
Here's how to attack it.

00:00:28.302 --> 00:00:30.467
Step one: cover the choices.

00:00:30.467 --> 00:00:32.117
They're built to tempt you.

00:00:32.117 --> 00:00:36.277
Step two: read the sentence before the blank, and the sentence with it.

00:00:36.277 --> 00:00:39.462
Step three: name the relationship in one word.

00:00:39.462 --> 00:00:40.567
Contrast?

00:00:40.567 --> 00:00:41.467
Result?

00:00:41.467 --> 00:00:42.427
Example?

00:00:42.427 --> 00:00:45.977
And step four: cross out every choice from the wrong group.

00:00:45.977 --> 00:00:48.067
Usually, only one survives.

00:00:49.122 --> 00:00:51.397
Learn the groups, not single words.

00:00:51.397 --> 00:00:55.182
Contrast words push against the last idea: however, but, yet.

00:00:55.182 --> 00:00:58.732
True anyway words mean despite that: nevertheless, still.

00:00:58.732 --> 00:01:02.212
Adding words keep going the same way: moreover, furthermore.

00:01:02.212 --> 00:01:05.372
Result words show a consequence: therefore, thus.

00:01:05.372 --> 00:01:09.407
Example words zoom in on one case: for example, for instance.

00:01:09.407 --> 00:01:13.145
And similarity words say the same again: similarly, likewise.

00:01:14.160 --> 00:01:15.310
Let's try one.

00:01:15.310 --> 00:01:16.860
Cover the choices.

00:01:16.860 --> 00:01:20.715
Sentence one: most desert plants store water in their leaves.

00:01:20.715 --> 00:01:24.590
Sentence two: the ocotillo drops its leaves entirely.

00:01:24.590 --> 00:01:27.885
That's the opposite, so the relationship is contrast.

00:01:27.885 --> 00:01:29.410
Now sort the choices.

00:01:29.410 --> 00:01:31.410
For instance gives an example.

00:01:31.410 --> 00:01:33.245
Similarly means the same.

00:01:33.245 --> 00:01:34.890
Therefore shows a result.

00:01:34.890 --> 00:01:37.165
However is the only contrast word.

00:01:37.165 --> 00:01:38.543
The answer is B.

00:01:39.606 --> 00:01:41.531
Watch out for the fancy word.

00:01:41.531 --> 00:01:44.381
Moreover and consequently sound impressive.

00:01:44.381 --> 00:01:47.336
But if the logic is contrast, they're wrong.

00:01:47.336 --> 00:01:49.283
Logic first, every time.

00:01:50.311 --> 00:01:52.486
Here's the whole lesson on one page.

00:01:52.486 --> 00:01:53.561
How to spot it.

00:01:53.561 --> 00:01:54.961
The four steps.

00:01:54.961 --> 00:01:56.231
The word groups.

00:01:56.231 --> 00:01:57.306
And the trap.

00:01:57.306 --> 00:02:00.139
Pause the video now, and copy it into your notes.
